---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import { engines, type EngineGuide } from "../../data/site";

export function getStaticPaths() {
  return engines.map((engine) => ({ params: { engine: engine.slug }, props: { engine } }));
}

interface Props { engine: EngineGuide }
const { engine } = Astro.props;
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
const coreRelease = "https://github.com/violetweather/Certael/releases";
---

<BaseLayout title={`${engine.name} ${engine.version} Certael installation guide`} description={`Install Certael Core and the optional Agent integration in ${engine.name} ${engine.version}.`}>
  <section class="page-hero shell">
    <p class="eyebrow">Engine guide / {engine.name}</p>
    <h1>{engine.name} <span class="gradient-text">{engine.version}</span></h1>
    <p class="lede">Install the prebuilt package, bootstrap a server-bound session, and protect the first authoritative action without compiling Certael native code.</p>
    <a class="button primary" href={coreRelease}>Download release ↗</a>
  </section>
  <section class="section-tight shell guide-layout">
    <nav class="guide-nav" aria-label={`${engine.name} guide sections`}>
      <a href="#download">01 / Download</a><a href="#install">02 / Install</a><a href="#session">03 / Session</a><a href="#action">04 / First action</a><a href="#agent">05 / Optional Agent</a><a href="#verify">06 / Verify</a>
    </nav>
    <div class="guide-content">
      <section id="download"><p class="eyebrow">01 / Download</p><h2>Use the published package.</h2><p>Download <code>{engine.artifact}</code> and <code>checksums-sha256.txt</code> from the same Certael release. Verify the archive before extracting it. A partially successful workflow is not a release.</p></section>
      <section id="install"><p class="eyebrow">02 / Install</p><h2>Place the adapter.</h2><p>{engine.installPath}</p><ul>{engine.notes.map((note) => <li>{note}</li>)}</ul></section>
      <section id="session"><p class="eyebrow">03 / Session</p><h2>Create a bound session.</h2><pre><code>{engine.snippet}</code></pre><p>The illustrative networking object is your existing authenticated multiplayer transport. It sends the ephemeral public key to a trusted game server, receives a short-lived ticket challenge, and relays the proof.</p></section>
      <section id="action"><p class="eyebrow">04 / First action</p><h2>Send intent, not results.</h2><p>Choose one server-owned action such as crafting, spending currency, activating an ability, or submitting racing input. Define a stable binary request schema. The client authorizes those exact request bytes; the server validates them against trusted state and commits the result atomically.</p><div class="callout">Never treat “signature valid” as the gameplay decision. It proves possession of a session key, not that a claim is honest.</div></section>
      <section id="agent"><p class="eyebrow">05 / Optional Agent</p><h2>Add it only where useful.</h2><p>Install Certael Agent separately and have it launch the exported game. The engine adapter relays its hello, a server-signed launch bundle, fresh challenges, and signed reports through inherited process handles. Leave Agent disabled for ordinary offline play.</p><a class="button secondary" href={`${base}agent/`}>Understand Agent</a></section>
      <section id="verify"><p class="eyebrow">06 / Verify</p><h2>Attack the integration.</h2><ul><li>Alter a payload after signing.</li><li>Replay, reorder, and duplicate an action.</li><li>Substitute the match, player, server, environment, or build.</li><li>Submit a valid signature over a dishonest request.</li><li>Confirm the server rejects invalid state without advancing or double-granting.</li></ul><a class="button primary" href="https://github.com/violetweather/Certael/blob/main/docs/testing.md">Open test guide ↗</a></section>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
